<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malojirao Nimbalkar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1896–1978</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Malojirao Mudhojirao Naik Nimbalkar IV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malojirao <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nimbalkar">Nimbalkar</a> was the last ruling Raja of Phaltan, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> princely state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>, from 1917 until it merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948. He had been active in the state's administration and in the movement for responsible government, and after the merger he served as a minister in the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a>.</p></div>
